I came to know Lojban by Wikipedia.
At the end of the article there is a link saying "The Logical Language Group
home page". Through it you get to www.lojban.org, on which it's said "This
page is user-maintained, and is not endorsed by the LLG". So I was confused:
"Where's the LLG, then?" I'm still wondering who they are and what they are
doing now for Lojban. Could they be what are called "academic lojbanists"?

-Vid


